# LAONEI'S TRANSLATED CALLS, under Laonei's own name — call.laonei.co.
#
# The call pages live in the book container (book/public/call.html) and were
# first reachable only as thexchange.app/book/call. Inside the Laonei app
# nobody sees the address, but the LINK is the product — it is what one
# person sends another, often somebody in China who has never heard of any of
# this — and a Laonei call arriving as a link to a different company's site
# is a link people hesitate over. So the same pages answer here too, at the
# root: call.laonei.co/call/<id>#<key>.
#
# Needs one DNS record, `call` → this box, at laonei.co's registrar. Until it
# exists Caddy cannot get a certificate for the name and says so in its log;
# every other site here carries on regardless.
#
# The video still signals through thexchange.app/book/lk (the ticket names
# it), which the page reaches cross-origin; only the pages and their API
# move. /lk here too, so a later switch of BOOK_PUBLIC is a .env change.
{$TOMSCODING_CALL_DOMAIN:call.localhost} {
	encode zstd gzip

	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "same-origin"
		-Server
	}

	# The bare name opens the start page.
	@root path /
	redir @root /call 302

	handle_path /lk/* {
		reverse_proxy livekit:7880
	}
	handle {
		reverse_proxy book:8080
	}
}
